            <ArticleTitle>[Ivabradine--a medical alternative for patients with chronic stable angina pectoris].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3991-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Procoralan (Ivabradine) is a novel, specific If--current inhibitor, inducing reduction in heart-rate through a direct effect on sinoatrial automaticity at rest and during exercise. Thereby the drug may prevent myocardial ischaemia. So far the indications for using Procoralan are the following: symptomatic treatment of chronic stable angina pectoris in patients with sinus rhythm, in whom betablockers are contraindicated or not tolerated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
